{"id":966,"slug":"i-vitelloni","title":"I vitelloni","year":1953,"country":"Italy","duration":108,"spine":246,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/966-i-vitelloni","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/f3607ad7b7db2693f75c93bde0b02f73/6eAAsMzssFNbNWVe0Oz1QqnGnHibGy_large.jpg","description":"Federico Fellini’s second outing as a solo director yielded his first commercial success, a clear-eyed portrait of five young men lingering in a postadolescent limbo, dreaming of adventure and escape from their small coastal town. Drawing on memories tucked between the childhood nostalgia of Amarcord and the big-city hangover of La dolce vita, Fellini crafts a semiautobiographical masterpiece of sharply drawn character sketches: of skirt-chasing Fausto, forced to marry a girl he has impregnated; Alberto, the perpetual child; Leopoldo, a writer thirsting for fame; and Moraldo, the conscience of the group. An Oscar nominee for best original screenplay, I vitelloni captures the lassitude and longing of its protagonists with comic insight and compassion. ","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Federico Fellini","slug":"federico-fellini"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Franco Interlenghi","role":"Moraldo","slug":"franco-interlenghi"},{"actor":"Alberto Sordi","role":"Alberto","slug":"alberto-sordi"},{"actor":"Franco Fabrizi","role":"Fausto","slug":"franco-fabrizi"},{"actor":"Leopoldo Trieste","role":"Leopoldo","slug":"leopoldo-trieste"},{"actor":"Riccardo Fellini","role":"Riccardo","slug":"riccardo-fellini"},{"actor":"Leonora Ruffo","role":"Sandra","slug":"leonora-ruffo"},{"actor":"Jean Brochard","role":"Fausto’s father","slug":"jean-brochard"},{"actor":"Claude Farell","role":"Olga, Alberto’s sister","slug":"claude-farell"},{"actor":"Carlo Romano","role":"Mr. Michele","slug":"carlo-romano"},{"actor":"Enrico Viarisio","role":"Sandra’s father","slug":"enrico-viarisio"},{"actor":"Paola Borboni","role":"Sandra’s mother","slug":"paola-borboni"}],"credits":[{"role":"Direc